      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mark-honman",
        "email": "158605850+mark-honman@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2025-09-24T11:59:23Z"
      },
      "message": "Post-review updates\n\nthere is one big question left to resolve: ACLIC + IMSIC configurations.\n\nWhat's clear is that due to AIA CSRind space being a fixed window, if ACLIC and IMSIC were both present they would need to share the AIA-defined ei-prefixed registers.\n\nBut the way I read the AIA spec, the interrupt files are described as internal to the IMSIC and I guess this is how people will implement it.\n\nIMO we should keep the original AIA eidelivery definition until we have a specification of how ACLIC and IMSIC could possibly be attached to the same hart.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "44a43caeef5d701fd36b960feed94e95693b3e01",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-fast-interrupt/git/trees/44a43caeef5d701fd36b960feed94e95693b3e01"
